- Pinned Java client 5.5.1 confirms that the 31 modeled request headers inherit `equals`/`hashCode` from `RpcRequestHeader`; only `ns`, `nsd`, `bname`, and `oway` participate. Added those nullable fields and wire mappings to the Rust headers, with equality/hash over the same base fields and ignored subclass payload.
- `UnlockBatchMqRequestHeader` is now distinct from the Lock type. `ConsumeMessageDirectlyResultRequestHeader` retains the inherited `bname` separately from its subclass `brokerName`.
- Added the invoked Java identity fixture and Rust coverage for all 31 request-header types. Sorted fixture case keys so independent JVM runs serialize deterministically. Fixture SHA-256: `4cc545d6d1fc0efdb2cdd74b6a1eb0cd0b00b98ad028766f8bd7d2c05bd75973`.
- Updated request-header initializers across Consumer, Core, Producer, Remoting examples, and the offline benchmark. Adjusted two tests for DTOs that correctly no longer expose structural equality.
- PASS: `cargo test --workspace --locked` under UTC; `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked`; strict all-target/all-feature workspace Clippy; Maven `verify` (37 scenarios, fixture checks and Java/Rust cross-decodes); comparator self-test and 37-scenario manifest validation; race/leak smoke (16 cases × 3); fuzz smoke (104 frame seeds, 10 message seeds, 1,824 mutations); release example build; workspace benchmark compilation; locked Cargo metadata; metadata/license/dependency and seven-package content checks; unique-ID fixture test under UTC and Asia/Taipei; formatting and diff checks.
